Rips_ClaimPayout
├── when the rip is not finalized
│   └── it should revert.
├── when recipient is zero address
│   └── it should revert.
├── when caller is not the recipient and has neither admin nor operator role
│   └── it should revert.
├── when start index is out of bounds
│   └── it should revert.
├── when all ranges in scope are already claimed
│   └── it should not transfer any funds.
└── when there are unclaimed ranges
    ├── it should mark processed ranges as claimed.
    ├── it should calculate correct payouts using the affine permutation.
    ├── when every claimed entry has zero payout
    │   ├── it should accrue the protocol fee for those entries.
    │   ├── it should mark the ranges as claimed.
    │   └── it should credit the referrer period volume.
    ├── when caller has admin role and recipient is a different address
    │   └── it should transfer the payout to the recipient.
    └── when caller has operator role and recipient is a different address
        └── it should transfer the payout to the recipient.
    ├── given the preset currency is native
    │   ├── when protocol fee is zero
    │   │   ├── it should transfer the full ETH payout to the recipient.
    │   │   └── it should emit a {PayoutClaimed} event.
    │   └── when protocol fee is greater than zero
    │       ├── it should transfer the fee in ETH to the fee recipient.
    │       ├── it should transfer the remaining ETH payout to the recipient.
    │       ├── it should emit a {ProtocolFeeAccrued} event.
    │       └── it should emit a {PayoutClaimed} event.
    └── given the preset currency is an ERC20 token
        ├── when protocol fee is zero
        │   ├── it should transfer the full token payout to the recipient.
        │   └── it should emit a {PayoutClaimed} event.
        └── when protocol fee is greater than zero
            ├── it should transfer the fee in tokens to the fee recipient.
            ├── it should transfer the remaining token payout to the recipient.
            ├── it should emit a {ProtocolFeeAccrued} event.
            └── it should emit a {PayoutClaimed} event.
